WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.559
Calendar Feeds let other calendar apps follow a calendar from your site, and

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:08.116
let you move events in and out as files.

00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:12.396
This video shows how to make a private subscription address, how to add

00:00:12.396 --> 00:00:16.288
it to Outlook, Google Calendar or a phone, and how to export and

00:00:16.288 --> 00:00:17.900
import a calendar file.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.912
People keep other calendars too, in Outlook, in Google Calendar, and on their phone.

00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:31.160
Copying events by hand between them never lasts.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:36.671
A subscription address lets those apps follow a calendar from your site, and

00:00:36.671 --> 00:00:38.936
keep it up to date by themselves.

00:00:38.936 --> 00:00:40.736
It runs in one direction:

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:42.710
the apps read your calendar.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.703
Files move events both ways.

00:00:45.703 --> 00:00:50.981
Export a calendar as a calendar file, or import one from another calendar.

00:00:50.981 --> 00:00:55.270
Events that are already there are updated, not added twice.

00:00:59.461 --> 00:01:02.464
Open Calendars, then Manage Calendars.

00:01:02.464 --> 00:01:06.831
On a calendar's Actions menu, choose Subscription address.

00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:10.503
A calendar has no address until you make one.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:15.303
Choose Make an address, and the secret address appears, ready to copy.

00:01:15.754 --> 00:01:21.095
Choose Copy, and paste it into Google Calendar, under Other calendars, From URL.

00:01:21.095 --> 00:01:24.510
In Outlook, use Add calendar, Subscribe from web.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.622
Phones have the same option.

00:01:26.622 --> 00:01:30.534
The app then shows the events, and keeps them up to date.

00:01:30.985 --> 00:01:35.167
Anyone who has the address can see the events, so share it only

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.865
with people you trust.

00:01:36.865 --> 00:01:40.683
Choose Make a new address, and the old one stops working.

00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:43.895
Remove the address, and the feed is turned off.

00:01:45.493 --> 00:01:48.283
Private events are never shown in full.

00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:53.058
When an event's Visibility is Private, others see only that the time is

00:01:53.058 --> 00:01:58.143
busy, and the feed writes it as busy time, without the title or the details.

00:02:02.343 --> 00:02:07.699
On the same Actions menu, Export .ics downloads the calendar as a calendar

00:02:07.699 --> 00:02:10.913
file, with its events and how they repeat.

00:02:12.522 --> 00:02:17.190
Import .ics adds the events of a calendar file, such as one exported

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.586
from Google Calendar or Outlook.

00:02:19.586 --> 00:02:22.172
Choose the file, and choose Import.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:29.719
A message says how many events were added, changed and left unchanged.

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:33.773
The calendar opens, with the three events of the file.

00:02:34.227 --> 00:02:38.226
Here is a newer version of the same file, with the vendor demo

00:02:38.226 --> 00:02:39.873
moved to the next day.

00:02:39.873 --> 00:02:41.167
Import it again.

00:02:41.623 --> 00:02:44.801
One event is changed, and two are unchanged.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:51.476
The vendor demo moved, and nothing was added twice, because events are matched by their identifier.

00:02:51.476 --> 00:02:54.273
Importing the same file twice is safe.

00:02:58.473 --> 00:03:04.248
The Calendar Feeds feature adds the subscription address, and the export and import.

00:03:04.248 --> 00:03:06.943
Imported events send no invitations.

00:03:07.693 --> 00:03:11.130
Make a new address if one is shared by mistake.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.983
The old address stops working at once.

00:03:14.733 --> 00:03:18.184
Following a calendar this way is one direction.

00:03:18.184 --> 00:03:23.264
Signing in to Google Calendar or Microsoft 365 to keep calendars in step

00:03:23.264 --> 00:03:25.413
both ways is not available.

00:03:27.413 --> 00:03:31.492
Make an address to let other apps follow a calendar, and use calendar

00:03:31.492 --> 00:03:33.559
files to move events in and out.

00:03:33.559 --> 00:03:34.973
Thanks for watching.

